# Internal working-memory files (development history, session handoff
# notes) -- kept locally, not published. See CLAUDE.md's own "Follow-up
# code review" section for why: no secrets in either file, but both carry
# far more internal narrative/process detail than a published repo needs,
# and HANDOFF.md in particular goes stale between sessions. Untracked here
# rather than deleted -- git rm --cached, not rm -- so they stay on disk
# for local/session use; existing git history still has prior committed
# versions (this doesn't retroactively scrub that).
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md

# Prompt Builder worksheet build tooling
profiles/worksheets/node_modules/
